I now see what you mean. I misunderstood your question.

Well, it works just like blessing multiple things. When you dip 20
potions of water into one potion of holy water, the one holy water is
consumed, and the 20 potions of water are blessed, becoming holy water.

All potions are of the same type. I guess it's because it circumvents
the problem that you'd need an extra slot in your inventory when all
a-zA-Z are already occupied. Also, it makes it a bigger gamble.

For example, if you have 20 potions of confusion, you could dip all of
them into a potion of gain energy, and have a 2/3 chance of ending up
with 20 potions of booze (not what you want), and only a 1/3 chance of
getting 20 potions of enlightenment (what you really want).

You could decide to dip 10 potions of confusion in a potion of gain
energy twice, and your chances of getting at least 10 potions of gain
energy would, of course, go up. However, this would cost you 2 potions
of gain energy in total, and thus would be more costly.

